rael’s monarchy, particularly during the reigns of Ahab and Jezebel, showing that the land assigned in Joshua’s day rem
ained central to Israel’s history. Cities provided places of administration, protection, trade, and public worship, whi
le villages sustained the daily agricultural life of the people. God’s careful distribution of the land established Isr
ael in Canaan as a people with homes, families, boundaries, and a shared calling to live faithfully before Him.
